          "Pochereth-hazzebaim’s descendants, Amon’s descendants."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          60
        ],
        "lines": [
          "All the temple servants",
          "and the descendants of Solomon’s servants 392."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          61
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The following are those who came from Tel-melah, Tel-harsha, Cherub, Addon, and Immer, but were unable to prove that their ancestral families and their lineage were Israelite:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          62
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Delaiah’s descendants,",
          "Tobiah’s descendants,",
          "and Nekoda’s descendants 642"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          63
        ],
        "lines": [
          "and from the priests: the descendants of Hobaiah, the descendants of Hakkoz, and the descendants of Barzillai #— #who had taken a wife from the daughters of Barzillai the Gileadite and who bore their name."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          64
        ],
        "lines": [
          "These searched for their entries in the genealogical records, but they could not be found, so they were disqualified from the priesthood."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          65
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The governor ordered them not to eat the most holy things until there was a priest who could consult the Urim and Thummim."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          66
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The whole combined assembly numbered 42,360"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          67
        ],
        "lines": [
          "not including their 7,337 male and female servants,",
          "as well as their 245 male and female singers."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          68
        ],
        "lines": [
          "They had 736 horses, 245 mules,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          69
        ],
        "lines": [
          "435 camels, and 6,720 donkeys."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          70
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Some of the family heads contributed to the project. The governor gave 1,000 gold coins, 50 bowls, and 530 priestly garments to the treasury."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          71
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Some of the family heads gave 20,000 gold coins and 2,200 silver minas to the treasury for the project."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          72
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The rest of the people gave 20,000 gold coins, 2,000 silver minas, and 67 priestly garments."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          73
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The priests, Levites, gatekeepers, temple singers, some of the people, temple servants, and all Israel settled in their towns."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
